WEBVTT

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.020
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.230
Onee-chan. It's morning already.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.180
Morning, Keiko.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.880
Honestly, Onee-chan. You always laze
 around the house like a fluffy, woolly blob.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.080
Fluffy...

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.410
If the alternative is almost getting 
hit by a truck while saving a kid,

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.820
then I'd rather you were all woolly 
when you go out too, but...

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.670
Sorry I scared you.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.640
By the way, Misato, what were you watching 
before you went to sleep last night?

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.320
It was <i>Stone-Age Boy, Giatrus</i>!

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.760
I really shouldn't watch it.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.390
It makes me want to eat meat.

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:10.070
Okay! Today, I'll hunt a mammoth
and bring it back for my daughter!

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.590
Papa, where'd you pull that stone axe from?

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.500
I can't drink monkey-made sake,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.020
but kuchikamizake from <i>Your Name.</i> made 
by a high school girl would be all right.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.340
I know what you mean!

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.780
What's with this otaku family?

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.790
Can we talk about something I understand, too?

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.960
<i>I didn't have any friends,</i>

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.280
<i>but surrounded by the warmth of my family,</i>

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.600
<i>I was more than happy enough.</i>

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.860
<i>And I know that even if I had 
never been reincarnated...</i>

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.350
It went by so quickly.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.140
Tomorrow we graduate from Eckland Academy.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.830
Indeed. Three years was a brief time.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.160
Did you hear that, Aureana?

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.170
They're talking like nothing at all 
happened in the last three years.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:24.180
Do they have any idea how much you and I got 
dragged around by the pair of them, Monika-san?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.530
She might seem domineering at first glance,
 but our Marcela-sama is deeply compassionate,

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.980
and never hesitates to dive into
 trouble to help someone.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.730
And then there's her chief counselor, who 
comes up with the most terrible schemes, Adele...

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.010
And us two, forever swept 
up in it! Sob, sob, sob...

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:45.880
And before we knew it, we were known as the 
"Wonder Four" throughout the academy...

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.700
Sob, sob, sob...

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.260
Monika-san, Aureana-san...

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.410
I-It was never my intention to...

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.910
I'm only joking.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:57.720
We're commoners, but you called 
us friends and treated us well.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.800
We'll treasure every experience we 
had with you these last three years.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.050
H-Honestly... Do you have to 
say such embarrassing things?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.140
But you're right.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:09.660
Adele-san...

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.690
Meeting you and being your friend is 
something I will always take pride in.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.150
So will I!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.280
Thanks to all of you,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.240
all the family disputes within 
Viscount Ascham's lands were resolved,

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.660
and I was able to avenge 
my mother and grandfather!

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.960
Even after we graduate, 
we'll always be friends, right?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.000
Of course!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.080
<i>Though our paths may part,</i>

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.220
<i>the happy days spent with my dearest friends</i>

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.090
<i>will continue on...</i>

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.170
<i>Even if I never went on adventures 
where my life was on the line...</i>

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.010
Or not.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.270
How long are these impossible dreams 
going to keep reality at bay...

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:55.600
...for us?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.600
But, I mean...

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.320
This is the first time since I reincarnated 
that anything like that has happened...

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.560
None of my attacks worked at all.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.960
It hurt so much...

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.710
When I think I might die again,
 I'm just so scared!

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.060
That's why you're not getting up?

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.840
I mean, it's an elder dragon...

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.440
It stands at the top of this world.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.340
My power is only half of its power.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.170
Without more power, there's no way I can win!

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.940
That's dumb.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:30.690
You're the one who asked for average abilities,

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.690
and now when it's down to the wire, 
you're all, "I want more power!"

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.180
That's just dumb.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.810
True. There doesn't seem much point to 
standing up if you're going to be like that.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.940
Hold on. Usually, in this sort of situation,
 if I tried to get up...

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.170
Stop! Stop that, Mile!

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.320
You'll really die this time!

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.100
...and while you try to stop me,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.000
Schumann's Piano Concerto in A minor, Opus 54
 would play in the background...

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.210
We don't need this.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:02.340
Without that accident, I could have 
been happy, even without reincarnating.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.090
If I'd been smarter about things,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.970
I could have stayed forever 
with the first friends I ever made.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.930
It's the same, even now.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.270
People think of me as a girl who's capable,

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:19.530
but in the end, nothing ever works out right!

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.000
Does that matter?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.150
Shouldn't we take this seriously?

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.870
I'm already done.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.070
Complaining now just puts me in a tough spot.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.600
Are you done, too?

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.580
Not as Adele von Ascham. In your life as Mile.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.000
My... My life as Mile...

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.080
Maximum Flame Sphere!

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.960
Even if the opponent's an elder dragon, 
Mile would never die so easily!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.260
That's right. She's just 
being a sleepyhead again!

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.550
So, until she wakes, we will protect Mile!

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.560
Reina-san... Pauline-san... Mavis-san...

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:03.340
Listen up. As long as crimson 
blood runs through our veins,

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.360
we will never betray our friends.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.570
Our friendship will never be destroyed!

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.980
The vow we swore that day...

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.520
That's right!

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.370
I... We are still...

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:25.710
You! You're all so weak. Why won't you give up?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.000
What are you trying to do here?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.800
An elder dragon controlling beastpeople...

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.470
Using them to excavate ruins 
of human civilizations!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.780
Inferior creatures getting above yourselves!

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.110
To think you could inflict 
this much damage on me.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:42.600
Maybe I'll just kill you 
like I did the first girl!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.190
Magic Seal!

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.110
Huh?

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:56.650
Did you just say you were 
going to kill my friends?

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:58.490
Y-You're...

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.880
Honestly! What took you so long?

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.540
You really do sleep in too much.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.970
As a knight, it's embarrassing 
to say this, but...

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.720
Get him, Mile!

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.310
You! Why aren't you dead?

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.470
And the strength of your magic 
just now! What was that?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.000
There's only one reason why you'll lose.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.730
There's just one simple answer.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.980
You made me angry.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.900
You're just a human!

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.890
My attack didn't work?

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.910
That's not possible!

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.370
What?

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:48.180
<i>Well, thinking about it logically, 
the answer is simple.</i>

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.200
Indeed.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.260
Mile-sama's thought waves are half as 
strong as the strongest elder dragon's.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.010
However...

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:59.010
<i>There must be all sorts of elder dragons, 
and not all of them can be at the top.</i>

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.580
When you first encountered the elder dragon,

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.980
you were caught off-guard, and afraid.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.310
That plus despair caused 
disruptions in your thought waves,

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.980
which the rage at the thought of your 
friends dying forced back into shape.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.770
In your current state, 
Mile-sama, you will surely...

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.530
There's no way I'll lose!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.110
Why? Why doesn't it work?

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:16.940
Magic energy, collect!

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:21.450
Pierce through! Spirit... no, Magic Gun!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.080
Now, I have a lot of questions for—huh?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:32.590
What?

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:38.230
What are you howling about, Wence?

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.600
My. There are humans here, too.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.310
Gulp!

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.080
Playing again, are you?

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:50.530
The honored eldest is always telling you 
not to mistreat those lesser than us.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.600
Huh? Could it be?

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:55.290
Were you the one being bullied?

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:01.330
An elder dragon being picked on by 
a human. It's just too amusing, Wence.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.950
<i>One was bad enough. Three is...</i>

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.200
Fastest on the draw wins!

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.520
Defense magic, now! Layer it!

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.300
I couldn't make it through...

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.760
What? That can't be! What was that?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.120
Human magic broke through 
elder dragon magic? <i>Our</i> magic?

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.720
Hyper Breath!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.390
Wait! That's going too far!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.520
Mile!

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.260
She took the Breath head-on
 and stood up afterward?

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.400
That can't be! What kind of human is she?

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.760
No matter what, I will protect my friends!

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.520
Let's go, Nano-chan. Lend me your strength!

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.160
Of course!

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:47.930
Magic energy, collect!

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.560
No matter what you try, it won't work!

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:56.590
We'll take whatever pathetic 
human magic you throw at us!

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.380
Go!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.260
It can't be! It's only a 
human's Fire Lance spell!

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.860
You seem to be under the wrong impression.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:12.270
That was no Fire Lance. It was 
low-level magic. Just a Fireball.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.520
What?

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:15.760
<i>It was actually a Fire Lance,</i>

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.380
<i>but if it upsets the elder dragons, 
I'll let them think it wasn't.</i>

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.610
<i>But I do feel like that attack 
was stronger than usual...</i>

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:25.360
Have you forgotten, Mile-sama?

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:27.980
When nanomachines are given clear directions,

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.700
the effectiveness of the magic can 
increase as much as 3.27 times.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.920
Three times stronger than normal! 
I like the sound of that!

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:38.440
What is with this girl? Is she really human?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.360
That's what I'd like to know!

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.560
Hey, everyone!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:47.010
If you'd all surrender and explain your 
plan to me, it'd really help a lot.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.200
Cease your prattling, human!

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.770
Full strength, everyone.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.110
There are three of you, but I have...

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.820
my life as high school girl Kurihara Misato,

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:03.020
my life as a young lady of 
noble birth, Adele von Ascham,

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:08.030
and my life now as C-Rank Hunter Mile!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.200
Magic energy charged to 120%!

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.790
Fire!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.670
She blocked it!

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.920
No! She can't!

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.800
What are you?

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.550
I am Mile of the Crimson Vow!

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:29.140
Just a normal girl, like you'd find anywhere!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.890
That's a lie!

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:52.910
Mile!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.400
Yes?

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.220
Is everyone okay?

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:01.640
Hold on a minute.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.300
How can you treat this so lightly?

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.980
Oh, those elder dragons sure 
were tough opponents...

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.940
I'm not talking about that!

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:12.560
Normally, even an army
 can't defeat an elder dragon.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.060
Who are you?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.000
<i>This reaction is normal.</i>

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.940
<i>Seeing a girl single-handedly 
defeat elder dragons...</i>

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.930
<i>Even Reina-san and the others must be...</i>

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:29.200
Huh? It should be perfectly 
obvious who Mile is.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.240
What?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.800
A washboard-flat pipsqueak...

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.290
...who seems grounded, but is 
actually scatterbrained...

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.380
...who considers herself common-sensical, 
even though she isn't at all.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.040
What?

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.070
So how can this girl defeat elder dragons?

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.800
That's obvious, isn't it?

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:48.390
A secret family technique. Right?

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.660
Guys!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:04.530
The backlash from overusing Micross!
 The pain! It's here!

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.650
Here. Healing magic.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:09.910
Oh, I'm all better.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.410
Wha? Girls!

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:17.130
Oh, all right. I won't ask about this anymore,

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.260
and I won't report it to the Guild.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:22.460
After all, my original mission was to 
investigate the strange phenomena in the forest,

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:31.680
which is why hearing what they 
have to say takes precedence here.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.800
That's true.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.420
Will you talk to us now?

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.560
Or do you want to go again?

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.560
What we seek is a lost civilization.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.020
A lost civilization?

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.160
You can't mean the prehistoric civilization?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.470
A legendary country said to 
have prospered long, long ago.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.050
The people didn't depend on magic, and yet,

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:55.600
information from distant lands, 
the depths of the sea, the sky...

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.280
Even the stars themselves... 
They controlled it all.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.040
There was no famine or war.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.020
It was even said to be the land of the gods.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.820
Huh. I see what you're saying,

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.600
but how could such an amazing 
civilization crumble?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.000
That's exactly why its existence is doubted.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.570
But if the elder dragons are searching for it,

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:17.220
then that lends much more credence to the theory.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.720
We would be too conspicuous 
if we worked out in the open.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:27.230
So we ordered the beastpeople to search for 
ruins and artifacts from the lost civilization.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.540
Then, is this place truly a ruin 
from the prehistoric civilization?

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:38.070
Unfortunately, this seems to have been created
 by later worshipers of the lost civilization.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.250
In other words, a failure.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.220
I see.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:44.750
Therefore, we will leave these lands.

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:49.510
The beastpeople, too, will encroach 
on this domain no longer.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.350
In which case, you are left 
with no difficulties, correct?

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:55.240
All right.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:59.020
<b>2
 
D
A
Y
S
 
L
A
T
E
R</b>

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.850
I am in your debt.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.130
No, we're in yours.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.480
Thanks for covering for us so well.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.770
I have the feeling we will meet again someday.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.240
Goodbye.

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:12.610
I heard all about it!

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:17.830
As long as the Crimson Vow is around, 
the Guild and the Kingdom of Tils are safe!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.290
Just leave it to us!

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.330
We're back!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.660
Welcome home, ladies!

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:31.090
I heard all about it! You guys pulled 
off something amazing again, right?

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:34.440
I know it's sudden, but do you think 
we could arrange a feast for tonight?

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.300
With no limits on the budget!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.930
Thanks for your patronage!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.810
<b>Baths</b>

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:45.810
I feel alive again!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.480
Dinner was fun, wasn't it?

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.990
The heat is getting to me. 
I really must be tired...

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.020
Should we get out then?

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.530
I'm going to stay a little longer.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.410
Keroron

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.660
All right.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.580
But can I ask you one thing?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.710
What is it?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:14.840
Why would this world's strongest creatures, 
the elder dragons, need the lost civilization?

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.500
I cannot tell you.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:23.980
Not even if it meant I must fight you again.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:25.640
Nano-chan...

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.400
Yes?

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.810
Do you know what the elder dragons are after?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:29.640
Yes.

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.000
What is it?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.590
That's classified information.

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:33.230
What?

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.550
We nanomachines receive wishes 
in the form of thought waves,

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:41.490
and grant them when it is within our 
power to do so. We are simply tools.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.830
But the question you just asked, Mile-sama,

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.100
involves classified information.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.170
Thus, your wish cannot be granted.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.640
Which means that the elder 
dragons' goal is something big,

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.300
something connected to that 
classified information.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.420
That's classified information.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:58.730
I'm sorry, Mile-sama.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.430
It's all right. Thanks.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.680
To be honest, the world you 
will be reborn into has had

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.120
many civilizations over time, 
all of which have collapsed.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:14.660
Even now, with the addition of nanomachines, 
there is no hope of further evolution.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:18.570
The result is a world that 
all of us have cast aside,

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.280
one that simply continues to scrape along.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:26.040
Why are you reincarnating me 
into such a difficult world?

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.460
We have our own circumstances to consider.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:33.110
A world with no gods?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.560
What's wrong?

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:51.940
Sorry! I had a weird dream.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.340
Is that all...

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.160
Are you all right? You seem tired.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.360
Sorry! I dozed off! I'm so sorry!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:14.460
Mile! Can you take the one
that headed your way?

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.180
Huh? What is this?

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.650
<i>I want to talk to them about these worries.</i>

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:50.740
<i>But that would mean telling them 
that I've been reincarnated.</i>

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:53.540
<i>I can't! I can't do that!</i>

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.660
<i>Thank you for everything you've done for me.</i>

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.140
<i>Please, take care of yourselves!</i>

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.650
Are you sure about this, Mile-sama?

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:26.160
<i>I always thought I wanted normal happiness.</i>

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:32.290
<i>But this world that I reincarnated into 
is much more unstable than I thought...</i>

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:37.790
<i>The elder dragons are hungry for the 
lost civilization, trying to start something.</i>

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.920
<i>It might not happen for a hundred years.</i>

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>But... it might also be tomorrow.</i>

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:47.900
<i>This world has no gods.</i>

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.220
<i>No god will save it.</i>

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:53.880
<i>I don't know what I can do, but...</i>

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:54.980
<i>I can't just ignore it.</i>

00:20:55.670 --> 00:21:01.130
<i>Because I've found something much 
more important than my own happiness.</i>

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.220
We haven't seen the school in a long time.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:05.360
No, we haven't.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.070
Huh?

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.580
Wh-Why are all of you here?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.490
What do you mean "why"?

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.710
It was so obvious you were 
worrying over something.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:18.330
B-But the three of you were asleep!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.500
We were pretending to sleep.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.130
What?

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:25.010
My princess, won't you consider 
engaging a knight's services?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.970
Wha? You look too beautiful like that!

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:32.970
Y-You can't! The journey I'm starting 
now is even more dangerous than before!

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.590
Does it matter?

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:35.230
Huh?

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:39.210
Of course we'll help you. We're your friends.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.120
But...

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.020
There's only one thing that's important to us.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.950
Mile, do you...

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.820
Being with us... Do you not like it?

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:56.500
Th-The answer to that should be obvious.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.480
I...

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.960
I want to stay with you!

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:00.790
Mile!

00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:06.120
Honestly, Mile!

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:09.520
Um, there's something I wanted 
to talk to you about...

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:10.800
What is it?

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:14.260
Why do you all sneak out on your own?

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:15.720
We're friends, aren't we?

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.560
Sorry!

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:21.190
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:21.190
<b>Didn't I Say The Crimson Vow Would Never Be Destroyed?!</b>

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:54.100
Okay! The Crimson Vow is setting 
off on a new adventure!

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:56.350
First, we'll aim to get to B Rank!

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:59.560
After that, I'll get to 
A Rank and become a knight!

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:02.560
I'll make lots of money and 
set up my own business firm.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:06.210
Um, first we need to investigate
 the elder dragons...

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:11.460
And I think I would like to gain a normal, 
average girl's happiness after all.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.900
The elder dragons? You won't even 
tell us the real reasons behind that.

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:17.610
We can tell right away when you're lying, Mile.

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:19.790
Which is why you are going 
to confess everything about

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:21.210
your secret family techniques, including that.

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:22.150
Huh?

00:23:22.150 --> 00:23:23.710
Let's do it!

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.000
Yeah!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.840
What? What?!

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.160
What?

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:30.800
Now, let's see...

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:35.560
Will Mile-sama ever be able 
to attain normal happiness?

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.850
That answer is...

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.100
classified information.
